presets.prompt:
Make colour variants of the master material {{selected_asset}} as instances in {{content_folder}}, one per entry of: {{variants}}
1. hyper_material_inspect the master (load it with Unreal MCP's asset tools if it reports asset_not_loaded): confirm a vector parameter named `{{colour_param}}` exists. If it does not, stop and tell me which parameter to expose.
2. One hyper_material_apply_plan (fresh OperationId, bDryRun false) with one create_material_instance per variant (8 at most): TargetPath the object path `{{content_folder}}/MI_<Master>_<Variant>.MI_<Master>_<Variant>`, ParentPath the master's object path, and a vector parameter `{{colour_param}}` set to the variant's linear colour. The tool reads each value back. If the reply is still pending, hyper_operation_wait with that OperationId. Change no other asset.
3. If props are selected in the level and the lighting_lookdev pack is available: hyper_lighting_inspect for the revision, then one hyper_lighting_apply_plan (fresh OperationId, bSave false) with one set_actor_material per prop (empty property, slot 0), variant i on prop i of: {{selected_actors}}
Then hyper_capture_view of the level viewport. Otherwise skip this step and say why.
Report a PASS/FAIL table: every instance exists at its path, its parent is the master, `{{colour_param}}` holds the requested colour, and each prop shows its variant. Then the capture on its own line as ![variants](absolute path).
